WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.370
There are hidden oil wells all over Los Angeles.

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:09.049
These secret oil wells are hidden right in
plain sight.

00:00:09.049 --> 00:00:11.320
Some next to schools and shopping malls.

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:15.280
Some are discretely concealed inside plain,
boring old office blocks.

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:18.529
These cleverly designed buildings are all
like “we’ve got nothing to hide”, but

00:00:18.529 --> 00:00:19.539
then, bang!

00:00:19.539 --> 00:00:20.539
Oil well.

00:00:20.539 --> 00:00:24.930
These discrete oil wells have produced millions
of barrels of crude oil over the years.

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:31.279
In the 1890s Los Angeles, then a small town
with a population of just 50,000, was a thriving

00:00:31.279 --> 00:00:32.450
oil field.

00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:35.420
The ground beneath the city is rich in petroleum.

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:40.220
By 1930, California was producing one quarter
of the world’s oil.

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:45.920
LA grew exponentially and it is now one of
the most densely populated cities in the world.

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:50.200
Most inhabitants are under the impression
that the oil industry that LA was built upon

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:53.890
has mostly dried up and operations ceased
long ago.

00:00:53.890 --> 00:00:56.820
But this couldn’t be further from the truth.

00:00:56.820 --> 00:01:02.210
The bustling city still produces oil at an
astonishing rate and every year more secret

00:01:02.210 --> 00:01:06.900
oil wells are built around the city, most
of the time the local residents have no idea

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:09.040
they are living near an oil well.

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:13.780
In the 30s when LA’s oil industry was booming
and people thought this sticky black crude

00:01:13.780 --> 00:01:19.650
was the next best thing since the invention
of canned beer, 95% of Los Angeles’ residents

00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:24.820
actually voted for a law that allowed oil
wells to be placed in one’s own back yard.

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:26.650
Can you imagine that today?

00:01:26.650 --> 00:01:31.420
Congressmen would be scalped and lynched by
an army of angry soccer mums at the slightest

00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:33.000
mention of such a law.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:39.560
But, because of that 1930s law, today every
quiet suburban LA neighbourhood has its very

00:01:39.560 --> 00:01:43.659
own penguin-killing, vegan-hating, black goldmine.

00:01:43.659 --> 00:01:49.909
The ability to hide oil wells, behind or inside
buildings is thanks to advances in technology

00:01:49.909 --> 00:01:55.229
which means oil wells are now significantly
smaller, quieter, more efficient and generally

00:01:55.229 --> 00:01:58.240
less messy than they were in the 20th century.

00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:03.430
Actually, due to advances in soundproofing
technology, urban oil wells are now almost

00:02:03.430 --> 00:02:04.820
completely silent.

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:10.560
As a result, oil wells have popped up in the
strangest of places amongst a metropolis of

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:16.130
3.9 million people, such as, smack bang in
the middle of residential areas, McDonald’s

00:02:16.130 --> 00:02:19.390
parking lots, and even a farmer’s market.

00:02:19.390 --> 00:02:24.209
Would you like some petroleum with your organic,
fairtrade, free-range avocados ma’am?

00:02:24.209 --> 00:02:26.290
What, you’ve never had free-range avocado?

00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:28.020
Some oil wells are in plain sight, others
cleverly concealed within the urban sprawl.

00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:33.220
So all this means that somewhere, in a boardroom,
in the headquarters of some giant oil corporation,

00:02:33.220 --> 00:02:37.959
there’s a group of men in suits, playing
a game of “where’s the most stupidly obvious,

00:02:37.959 --> 00:02:41.990
yet surprisingly deceptive place we can hide
an oil well?”, “What’s that Mike?

00:02:41.990 --> 00:02:44.819
In a playground disguised as a climbing frame?

00:02:44.819 --> 00:02:46.129
That’s genius!

00:02:46.129 --> 00:02:49.550
You win ‘child-hating oil baron of the month’
award”.

00:02:49.550 --> 00:02:53.940
But some haven’t even bothered to cleverly
blend into the surrounding environment.

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:58.300
Some take the other approach of, if we erect
a tall building with a suspicious lack of

00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:02.849
markings or branding on it, I bet nobody will
notice it’s an oil well.

00:03:02.849 --> 00:03:07.970
Today there are over 3,000 active oil wells
in Los Angeles, and more are sneakily built

00:03:07.970 --> 00:03:10.469
by urban oil ninjas ever year.

00:03:10.469 --> 00:03:14.660
Like this one that was built directly in the
schoolyard of one of the poshest schools in

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:20.450
the country, schooling the little tyrants
of the filthy rich, at Beverly Hills High

00:03:20.450 --> 00:03:21.450
School.

00:03:21.450 --> 00:03:24.830
But they painted some flowers on it and named
it the “Tower of Hope” so they could be

00:03:24.830 --> 00:03:26.349
all like “Oil well!

00:03:26.349 --> 00:03:29.129
There’s no oil well over here…”.

00:03:29.129 --> 00:03:34.330
The company behind this particular well, Venoco
has to pay leasing royalties to the high school

00:03:34.330 --> 00:03:35.629
every year.

00:03:35.629 --> 00:03:41.510
So much in fact that 85% of the school teacher’s
wages come from this oil money.

00:03:41.510 --> 00:03:44.489
Okay, now this one isn’t even trying to
hide.

00:03:44.489 --> 00:03:49.420
These “thoughtfully” placed wells are
inside a cemetery near Signal Hill.

00:03:49.420 --> 00:03:54.420
I suppose they’re hoping the decomposing
bodies will contribute to the oil supply.

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:58.080
So I guess that’s eco-friendly, kind of
like recycling?

00:03:58.080 --> 00:04:00.120
Oh, what’s that?

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:03.909
It takes a few million years to make fossil
fuel from dead bodies?

00:04:03.909 --> 00:04:27.800
Oh well, sorry guys, Rest 
in Petroleum.

